            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say “a palace,” then “I will read or study.” (Prāsādaḥ; paṭhiṣyāmi.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice: answer before the check",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No Sanskrit model is shown before you answer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 12,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 12s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You are a student reading a school timetable. Ask when the exam will be. Answer that it will be tomorrow. State that you will do the homework and study the lesson. Then name the teacher, classroom, mark, and answer words that belong to this school setting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built: check after speaking",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A complete response has four connected turns and the setting words. One check is परीक्षा कदा भविष्यति? श्वः परीक्षा भविष्यति। गृहकार्यं करिष्यामि। पाठं पठिष्यामि। Then recall विद्यालयः, छात्रः, अध्यापकः, समयसारणी, कक्षा, अंकः, उत्तरम्."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What held the old school words together? (One timetable question, its answer, and two first-person plans.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
